1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
Have you ever taken a sickie?
你曾经请过（一天的）病假吗？

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:05,460
If so, what did you say to your boss?
如果是的话，你对老板说了什么？

3
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:10,400
It seems many people in the UK like to blame their pets for their absence.
似乎许多英国人喜欢把缺勤的责任推给他们的宠物。

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,850
One person said they couldn't come to work because their rabbit was missing.
有个人说他们不能来上班，因为他们的兔子不见了。

5
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:19,880
Perhaps that was a white lie; this next one though sounds more like a porky.
也许那是个无恶意的谎话；不过接下来这个听起来更像是个谎话。

6
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:24,990
A worker said that he couldn't come to work because he had to take his dog to the vet.
一名员工说他不能来上班，因为他得带他的狗去看兽医（veterinary的简写）。

7
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:32,830
This might seem reasonable - apart from the fact that the man told his boss his dog was dead as a previous excuse for skiving off.
这听起来可能很合理——除了他曾经以他的狗死了为借口偷懒这件事之外。

8
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:40,580
If you've ever worked as a teacher, you'll know that children can be very creative when it comes to excuses for not doing their homework.
如果你曾经当过老师，你会知道孩子们在找借口不写作业时非常有创意。

9
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:43,700
Once again, it's popular to blame pets.
再一次，把责任推给宠物是很受欢迎的做法。

10
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:49,560
According to a BBC survey, almost 10 percent of excuses involve pets eating the assignment.
根据BBC的一项调查，几乎10%的借口涉及宠物吃掉了作业。

11
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:56,360
"The dog ate my homework" is a legendary excuse - no one is sure if a student has ever really used it.
“狗吃了我的作业”是一个非常著名的借口——没人确定是否有学生真的用过这个借口。

12
00:00:56,360 --> 00:01:00,590
But it's not just workplaces and schools which attract fibbers.
但不仅仅是工作场所和学校会吸引说小谎者。

13
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:06,230
People caught claiming welfare benefits illegally have also tried to con the authorities.
那些被抓住非法申领福利金的人也试图欺骗当局。

14
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:15,800
A husband whose wife was working while also on the dole said that he didn't know she had a job because he was always in the garden shed during working hours.
一个妻子在工作的同时也在领取救济金，她丈夫说，他不知道她有工作，因为在工作时间，他总是在花园棚屋里。

15
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:21,410
There are many more ridiculous excuses people have made for not doing the things they were supposed to do.
人们为了不做他们应该做的事情编造了更多荒谬的借口。

16
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:24,430
But there isn't enough room on this page to fit them all.
但这页纸的空间不足以容纳所有借口。

17
00:01:24,430 --> 00:01:29,390
And besides, I can't carry on because… the cat's eaten my keyboard.
而且，我也不能继续写下去了，因为……猫吃了我的键盘。

18
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:32,500
What about you: what's your excuse?
你呢：你的借口是什么？
